an></span></li><li>reduces the risk of heart disease</li><li>better <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t2-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> reduces the risk of accidents</li><li>improves <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t2-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> function by making it work faster</li><li>improves participants’ general well-being</li><li>gives people more <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t2-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> to take exercise</li><li>can lessen the feeling of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t2-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>, very common in older people</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits of Zumba:</strong></p><ul><li>A study at The University of Wisconsin showed that doing Zumba for 40 minutes uses up as many <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t2-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> as other quite intense forms of exercise.</li><li><em>The American Journal of Health Behavior</em>&nbsp;study showed that:</li></ul><p>–&nbsp; women suffering from <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t2-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;benefited from doing Zumba.</p><p>–&nbsp; Zumba became a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c16-t2-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;for the participants.</p></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-it